<section class="example-section">
  <h2 id="shell-heading">Create a bootable Alpine Linux USB drive</h2>

<p>These instructions are based off <a href="https://wiki.alpinelinux.org/wiki/Create_a_Bootable_Device" target="_blank">this guide</a> using the manual process outlined in <code>Manually copying Alpine files</code>:</p>

{{#> important-callout}}
<p>You have to run the commands as root <code>sudo</code> from a linux system like Ubuntu.</p>
<p>One of the steps requires you to reference the ISO as a cdroom, you can simply run:</p>
{{/important-callout}}

{{#> code-block}}
sudo mkdir -p /media/cdroom
sudo mount -o loop,ro /path/to/image.iso /media/cdroom
{{/code-block}}
</section>
